Why: the letterhead quote templates (app/templates/reports/*_quote.html, styled by app/static/css/report.css) name
Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif. Linux servers have no Arial — prod's fontconfig hands back DejaVu Sans (RT11 §3.0, 23 Oct
2026) — and Arial's licence does not allow shipping its files. Liberation Sans has Arial's metrics (the same character
widths, so the same line and page breaks). report.css loads these files with @font-face and names them FIRST, so the
quote renders in the same faces on prod, CI and Windows. backend/tests/test_rt11_letterhead.py asserts the embedded
faces of every rendered quote are exactly these.
